1
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:19,000
[Quartermain]
KING SOLOMON'S MINES--

2
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:21,000
LIKE MANY OTHERS, WELL...

3
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:23,000
I DIDN'T BELIEVE IN THEM.

4
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:27,000
IN THOSE DAYS, AFRICA WAS A
LAND OF MANY ROMANTIC LEGENDS.

5
00:02:27,000 --> 00:02:31,000
IT HAD A VAST,
UNEXPLORED INTERIOR.

6
00:02:31,000 --> 00:02:35,000
I WAS A HUNTER AND IT WASN'T
UNTIL THE YEAR 1881

7
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:40,000
THAT I LEARNT THAT THE MINES
WERE A STARK REALITY.

8
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:45,000
I SAY "WERE" BECAUSE THEY
NOW LIE BURIED UNDER A MILLION
TONS OF ASHES AND LAVA.

9
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:49,000
AT THE TIME I'M SPEAKING OF,
DIAMONDS HAD BEEN
FOUND IN KIMBERLEY.

10
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:54,000
MANY ADVENTUROUS SPIRITS
FROM ALL PARTS OF THE WORLD...

11
00:04:01,000 --> 00:04:03,000
YOU'VE STRUCK
LUCKY AGAIN, RED.

12
00:04:03,000 --> 00:04:04,000
YES.

13
00:04:04,000 --> 00:04:06,000
YOU CAN COUNT YOUR
MONEY TOMORROW.

14
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:08,000
I'LL HAVE 5 POUNDS
ON ACCOUNT TO
GET DRUNK WITH.

15
00:04:08,000 --> 00:04:10,000
[Laughing]

16
00:04:10,000 --> 00:04:13,000
GET YOUR BACKS TO
THE WALL, THE WHOLE
BOILING LOT OF YOU.

17
00:04:13,000 --> 00:04:15,000
DON'T SHOOT, BOYS.
IT ISN'T A HOLD-UP.

18
00:04:15,000 --> 00:04:18,000
I'M JUST TENDING
MESELF AND THE
TREASURES OF ARABIE.

19
00:04:18,000 --> 00:04:20,000
CAST AN EYE OVER THAT,
ME BOY, AND SEE WHAT
YOU MAKE OF IT.

20
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:22,000
WHAT HAVE
YOU FOUND?

21
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:24,000
A HOUSE, CARRIAGE
AND PAIR FOR
ME DAUGHTER

22
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:27,000
AND THE LIFE OF
RILEY HEREAFTER
AND EVERMORE.

23
00:04:27,000 --> 00:04:31,000
DID YOU EVER
SEE THE LIKE?

24
00:04:31,000 --> 00:04:33,000
A NICE PIECE OF
CRYSTAL, O'BRIEN,

25
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:35,000
BUT NO DIAMOND.

26
00:04:35,000 --> 00:04:37,000
YOU DON'T
MEAN IT?

27
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:38,000
I'M SORRY,
MISS KATE.

28
00:04:38,000 --> 00:04:40,000
THAT'S BAD LUCK,
PATRICK, BAD LUCK.

29
00:04:40,000 --> 00:04:43,000
BAD LUCK NOTHING.
I WAS ONLY HAVING
A JOKE WITH YOU.

30
00:04:43,000 --> 00:04:46,000
COME ON, GIRL.

31
00:04:46,000 --> 00:04:51,000
[Donkey braying]

32
00:04:51,000 --> 00:04:53,000
TRY AGAIN, PATSY.

33
00:04:53,000 --> 00:04:56,000
DEVIL I WILL.
I SPURN THE DIAMOND
FIELDS UNDER ME SHOES.

34
00:04:56,000 --> 00:04:59,000
IF WE COULD ONLY GET
TO THE COAST, I COULD
GET A JOB TEACHING.

35
00:04:59,000 --> 00:05:00,000
AND WOULD
YOU LIKE IT?

36
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:01,000
I WOULD NOT.

37
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:03,000
[O'Brien]
OF COURSE
YOU WOULDN'T.

38
00:05:03,000 --> 00:05:06,000
LISTEN, THERE WAS A
MAN IN THE BAR LAST
NIGHT FROM THE CONGO.

39
00:05:06,000 --> 00:05:08,000
HE SAYS THERE'S
A FORTUNE IN IVORY.

40
00:05:08,000 --> 00:05:11,000
THERE'S BEEN A FORTUNE
IN EVERYTHING WE'VE TRIED,

41
00:05:11,000 --> 00:05:13,000
BUT IT WASN'T US
WHO FOUND IT.

42
00:05:13,000 --> 00:05:15,000
FROM NOW ON, WE'LL BE DECENT,
RESPECTABLE CITIZENS,

43
00:05:15,000 --> 00:05:18,000
AND WE'RE GOING TO THE COAST
BEFORE I CHANGE ME MIND.

44
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:20,000
HOW MUCH MONEY HAVE WE?

45
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:23,000
LESS THAN A POUND
AND ALL OUR TRAPS
ARE IN THE PAWNSHOP.

46
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:25,000
WHAT'S THAT
YOU HAVE?

47
00:05:25,000 --> 00:05:30,000
FOR YOU, A GIFT I
BOUGHT TO CELEBRATE OUR
MAGNIFICENT DISCOVERY.

48
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:31,000
A SHAMROCK!

49
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:34,000
FOR LUCK.
IT DIDN'T
COST A THING.

50
00:05:34,000 --> 00:05:36,000
I KNOW WHAT
IT COST.

51
00:05:36,000 --> 00:05:38,000
THERE WERE TWO
IN MULLIGAN'S STORE.

52
00:05:38,000 --> 00:05:40,000
HERE'S THE
OTHER FOR YOU.

53
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:42,000
KATHY, ME GIRL,
THERE WAS NEVER
ANYTHING TO BEAT IT.

54
00:05:42,000 --> 00:05:46,000
WITH A BIT OF SHAMROCK
APIECE, THERE'S NOTHING ON
EARTH CAN HOLD US DOWN.

55
00:05:46,000 --> 00:05:48,000
LOOK!

56
00:05:48,000 --> 00:05:51,000
GLORY BE TO GOD,
STRAIGHT FROM HEAVEN.

57
00:05:51,000 --> 00:05:53,000
ASK HIM FOR A LIFT
TO THE COAST.

58
00:05:53,000 --> 00:05:55,000
IT'S A 5-WEEK JOURNEY.
IT'S A LOT TO ASK.

59
00:05:55,000 --> 00:06:00,000
AND YOU CALL YOURSELF
AN IRISHMAN?

60
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:03,000
IT'S A FINE MORNING.

61
00:06:03,000 --> 00:06:05,000
[O'Brien]
IT'S A FINE MORNING.

62
00:06:05,000 --> 00:06:06,000
IS IT?

63
00:06:06,000 --> 00:06:08,000
IT IS.

64
00:06:08,000 --> 00:06:09,000
ARE YOU GOING
TO THE COAST?

65
00:06:09,000 --> 00:06:11,000
NO, KITSFONTEIN.

66
00:06:11,000 --> 00:06:14,000
WELL, THAT'S ALL
ON THE WAY.

67
00:06:14,000 --> 00:06:16,000
WHOSE WAY?

68
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:19,000
OURS.
WE WERE WONDERING
IF YOU'D GIVE US A LIFT.

69
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:21,000
NO.

70
00:06:21,000 --> 00:06:24,000
ME NAME IS KATHLEEN O'BRIEN,
AND THIS IS ME FATHER,
PATRICK O'BRIEN,

71
00:06:24,000 --> 00:06:26,000
BACHELOR OF ARTS,
TRINITY COLLEGE, DUBLIN.

72
00:06:26,000 --> 00:06:27,000
THANK YOU.

73
00:06:27,000 --> 00:06:29,000
BACHELOR OF ARTS AT
TRINITY COLLEGE, DUBLIN!

74
00:06:29,000 --> 00:06:32,000
A DOWN-AND-OUT
FROM THE DIGGINGS, HUH?

75
00:06:32,000 --> 00:06:34,000
WE'RE DOWN
BUT WE'RE NOT OUT.

76
00:06:34,000 --> 00:06:36,000
[Quartermain]
YOU'RE OUT AS FAR AS
MY WAGON'S CONCERNED.

77
00:06:36,000 --> 00:06:38,000
OH! SO YOU DON'T
APPROVE OF US?

78
00:06:38,000 --> 00:06:42,000
I DON'T APPROVE OF TEARING
UP THE FACE OF THE
COUNTRY FOR GREED.

79
00:06:42,000 --> 00:06:45,000
ME DAUGHTER IS
A GOOD COOK.

80
00:06:45,000 --> 00:06:47,000
I HAVE A GOOD COOK.

81
00:06:47,000 --> 00:06:48,000
ME FATHER'S A
WONDER TO TALK.

82
00:06:48,000 --> 00:06:50,000
YEAH, HE WOULD BE.

83
00:06:50,000 --> 00:06:52,000
[Kathy]
AND HE'S A LOVELY
RIFLE SHOT.

84
00:06:52,000 --> 00:06:54,000
JUST THINK OF THE GAME
HE COULD GET FOR YOU.

85
00:06:54,000 --> 00:06:59,000
[Laughter]

86
00:06:59,000 --> 00:07:00,000
WHAT'S FUNNY
IN THAT?

87
00:07:00,000 --> 00:07:02,000
QUARTERMAIN, BEST
HUNTER IN AFRICA.

88
00:07:02,000 --> 00:07:03,000
THAT ENDS IT.

89
00:07:03,000 --> 00:07:07,000
IT DOES NOT.

90
00:07:07,000 --> 00:07:10,000
MR. QUARTERMAIN,
YOU NEEDN'T TAKE US
IF YOU DON'T WANT TO,

91
00:07:10,000 --> 00:07:13,000
BUT HERE'S SOMETHING
FOR YOU TO THINK ABOUT IN
YOUR PRECIOUS SOLITUDE:

92
00:07:13,000 --> 00:07:16,000
ME FATHER'S OWN SISTER
IS DYING IN KILKENNY

93
00:07:16,000 --> 00:07:19,000
AND IF THEY NEVER MEET
THIS SIDE OF THE GATES,

94
00:07:19,000 --> 00:07:22,000
'TIS YOU THAT WILL
HAVE PREVENTED THEM.

95
00:07:22,000 --> 00:07:27,000
JUMP UP.

96
00:07:32,000 --> 00:07:37,000
♪[Spiritual singing]

97
00:07:59,000 --> 00:08:00,000
HOW MUCH LONGER?

98
00:08:00,000 --> 00:08:03,000
ANOTHER 10 DAYS.

99
00:08:03,000 --> 00:08:05,000
LOOK!

100
00:08:05,000 --> 00:08:07,000
[Kathy]
AH, THE PRETTY CREATURE.

101
00:08:07,000 --> 00:08:09,000
YOU STARTLED HER.

102
00:08:09,000 --> 00:08:11,000
MAYBE SHE KNOWS
THAT IN 10 DAYS

103
00:08:11,000 --> 00:08:14,000
YOU'LL BE AFTER
HER WITH YOUR
MURDERING GUNS.

104
00:08:14,000 --> 00:08:16,000
I'LL GET YOU
A KNIFE.

105
00:08:16,000 --> 00:08:17,000
YOU DON'T
LIKE HUNTING?

106
00:08:17,000 --> 00:08:18,000
NO, I DO NOT.

107
00:08:18,000 --> 00:08:20,000
NEITHER DO I.

108
00:08:20,000 --> 00:08:22,000
THEN WHAT DO YOU HUNT FOR?

109
00:08:22,000 --> 00:08:25,000
A LIVING. IT PAYS ME
TO RUN HUNTING TRIPS.

110
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:26,000
I'VE GOT 2
CLOWNS WAITING
FOR ME NOW.

111
00:08:26,000 --> 00:08:29,000
THERE MUST BE A LOT
OF MONEY IN HUNTING.

112
00:08:29,000 --> 00:08:32,000
I'VE BEEN THINKING OVER WHAT
THAT FELLA SAID ABOUT IVORY.

113
00:08:32,000 --> 00:08:35,000
HAVE YOU HAD
ANY EXPERIENCE
IN TRACKING GAME?

114
00:08:35,000 --> 00:08:37,000
HE ONCE TOOK PART
IN A BADGER HUNT,
BUT THE BADGER ESCAPED.

115
00:08:37,000 --> 00:08:39,000
YOU DON'T KNOW
WHAT YOU CAN DO
TILL YOU TRY.

116
00:08:39,000 --> 00:08:42,000
WHILE YOU'RE TRYING,

117
00:08:42,000 --> 00:08:45,000
YOUR POOR SISTER'S
PEACEFULLY PASSING
AWAY IN KILKENNY.

118
00:08:45,000 --> 00:08:49,000
ALAN QUARTERMAIN, IT WAS A
LIE ABOUT ME FATHER'S SISTER.

119
00:08:49,000 --> 00:08:51,000
I KNOW, I'VE MET
THE IRISH BEFORE.

120
00:08:51,000 --> 00:08:53,000
I'M GLAD YOU OWNED UP.

121
00:08:53,000 --> 00:08:55,000
AND WHY
SHOULDN'T SHE?

122
00:08:55,000 --> 00:08:58,000
SHE'S GONNA
SETTLE DOWN AND
TEACH SCHOOL.

123
00:08:58,000 --> 00:09:00,000
YOU'RE GOING
TO SETTLE DOWN?

124
00:09:00,000 --> 00:09:04,000
OF COURSE
I AM.

125
00:09:04,000 --> 00:09:09,000
I SUPPOSE THERE ISN'T ANYTHING
IN THE IVORY TRADE IS THERE?

126
00:09:09,000 --> 00:09:14,000
IF YOU ASK ME, THERE ISN'T A
PIN TO CHOOSE BETWEEN YOU.

127
00:09:17,000 --> 00:09:19,000
THERE'S A WAGON
ACROSS THE RIVER.

128
00:09:19,000 --> 00:09:21,000
NO. ANTELOPE
PROBABLY.

129
00:09:21,000 --> 00:09:22,000
I'M SURE
IT'S A WAGON.

130
00:09:22,000 --> 00:09:23,000
CAN'T BE.

131
00:09:23,000 --> 00:09:25,000
AND WHY NOT?

132
00:09:25,000 --> 00:09:28,000
THERE'S NOTHING
ACROSS THAT
RIVER BUT DEVILS.

133
00:09:28,000 --> 00:09:30,000
THAT'S WHAT
THE NATIVES SAY.

134
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:34,000
IT'S UNEXPLORED LAND,
DESERT PROBABLY.

135
00:09:34,000 --> 00:09:39,000
IT MAY BE THE DEVIL'S,
BUT I CAN SEE A WAGON.

136
00:09:42,000 --> 00:09:45,000
COME ON!

137
00:09:45,000 --> 00:09:50,000
[Shouting]

138
00:09:54,000 --> 00:09:55,000
TAKE THIS.

139
00:09:55,000 --> 00:09:57,000
WATER, QUICK!
WHOSE WAGON IS THIS?

140
00:09:57,000 --> 00:09:58,000
HE'S NOT
ABLE TO TALK.

141
00:09:58,000 --> 00:10:00,000
IT'S THE
DESERT.

142
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:05,000
INSIDE.

143
00:10:06,000 --> 00:10:11,000
[Man whispering]

144
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:17,000
[Shouting in foreign language]

145
00:10:19,000 --> 00:10:21,000
THAT'S ALL RIGHT,
THEY'RE LOOKING
AFTER HIM.

146
00:10:21,000 --> 00:10:24,000
THE OTHERS RAN AWAY IN
THE NIGHT MANY DAYS AGO.
THE FEAR WAS ON THEM.

147
00:10:24,000 --> 00:10:26,000
SURE, THE DEVIL.

148
00:10:26,000 --> 00:10:28,000
HE FELL ILL.
WE COULD NOT
REACH THE NORTH.

149
00:10:28,000 --> 00:10:29,000
HELP HIM
BACK TO CAMP.

150
00:10:29,000 --> 00:10:31,000
I TURNED BACK.
HE DOES NOT KNOW.

151
00:10:31,000 --> 00:10:33,000
LET ME GO ON.
OUT OF THE WAY.

152
00:10:33,000 --> 00:10:35,000
YOU CAN'T GO ON.
YOU ARE ILL.

153
00:10:35,000 --> 00:10:37,000
DO I CARE IF I AM ILL?

154
00:10:37,000 --> 00:10:38,000
I DON'T KNOW WHERE
YOU'RE GOING BUT--

155
00:10:38,000 --> 00:10:43,000
YOU WANT TO KNOW WHERE
I'M GOING BUT I TELL YOU,
YOU CANNOT FOLLOW.

156
00:10:43,000 --> 00:10:48,000
I CROSSED THE DESERT.
AFTER THE DESERT, I FIND
KING SOLOMON'S MOUNTAIN.

157
00:10:48,000 --> 00:10:52,000
AFTER THE MOUNTAIN,
I FIND KING SOLOMON'S MINES.

158
00:10:52,000 --> 00:10:54,000
DIAMONDS.

159
00:10:54,000 --> 00:10:59,000
SYLVESTRA, WHEN
YOU SEE ME AGAIN,

160
00:10:59,000 --> 00:11:02,000
I'LL BE THE RICHEST
MAN ON EARTH.

161
00:11:02,000 --> 00:11:06,000
SO, OUT OF THE WAY!

162
00:11:06,000 --> 00:11:10,000
[Mumbling incoherently]

163
00:11:10,000 --> 00:11:15,000
[Gasping]

164
00:11:19,000 --> 00:11:22,000
DID YOU HEAR THAT?
THE MINES OF KING
SOLOMON OVER THE DESERT.

165
00:11:22,000 --> 00:11:23,000
IS IT TRUE?

166
00:11:23,000 --> 00:11:26,000
TRUE, WE HAVE
HEARD OF THE MINES.

167
00:11:26,000 --> 00:11:27,000
[Quartermain]
GET ME SOME WATER.

168
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:29,000
[Speaking Kukuana]

169
00:11:29,000 --> 00:11:31,000
ALL THE JEWELS OF OPHRAH
AND NO ONE EVER DISCOVERED
WHERE OPHRAH WAS.

170
00:11:31,000 --> 00:11:32,000
THAT'S WHERE
IT IS MAYBE.

171
00:11:32,000 --> 00:11:34,000
[Quartermain]
KATHY! MY
MEDICINE CHEST.

172
00:11:34,000 --> 00:11:39,000
ALL RIGHT.

173
00:11:46,000 --> 00:11:51,000
[Speaking Kukuana]

174
00:11:53,000 --> 00:11:54,000
WHAT'S THAT YOU HAVE?

175
00:11:54,000 --> 00:11:55,000
A MAP.

176
00:11:55,000 --> 00:11:57,000
LOOK, 300
YEARS OLD.

177
00:11:57,000 --> 00:12:00,000
HE SAID A MAN
WENT THERE AND
NEVER CAME BACK.

178
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:03,000
LOOK, THE WAY
ACROSS THE DESERT

179
00:12:03,000 --> 00:12:06,000
AND HERE, KING SOLOMON'S
MOUNTAIN AND THE MINE.

180
00:12:06,000 --> 00:12:10,000
THE JEWELS OF OPHRAH,
THE GREATEST TREASURE
IN THE WORLD!

181
00:12:10,000 --> 00:12:13,000
NOW, THAT MAP IS HIS.
YOU HAD NO RIGHT
TO TAKE IT.

182
00:12:13,000 --> 00:12:16,000
I KNOW, BUT IF HE
LIVES WE WON'T USE IT,
AND IF HE DOESN'T,

183
00:12:16,000 --> 00:12:20,000
I'LL SEEK THE TREASURE
MESELF AND I'LL HAVE
MASSES SAID FOR HIS SOUL.

184
00:12:20,000 --> 00:12:23,000
THE SHAMROCK! I SAID
IT'D BRING US LUCK.

185
00:12:23,000 --> 00:12:25,000
[Quartermain]
KATHY!

186
00:12:25,000 --> 00:12:30,000
I'M COMING.

187
00:12:32,000 --> 00:12:33,000
DIG A GRAVE.

188
00:12:33,000 --> 00:12:37,000
[Speaking Kukuana]

189
00:12:37,000 --> 00:12:42,000
♪[Chanting]

190
00:12:44,000 --> 00:12:45,000
ALL OVER?

191
00:12:45,000 --> 00:12:48,000
GOD REST HIS SOUL.

192
00:12:48,000 --> 00:12:53,000
KATHY ASLEEP?

193
00:12:54,000 --> 00:12:57,000
IT MUST BE TERRIBLE TO
DIE ALONE IN THE DESERT
WITHOUT YOUR FOLKS.

194
00:12:57,000 --> 00:12:59,000
TERRIBLE.

195
00:12:59,000 --> 00:13:02,000
WHAT DID YOU
THINK OF THE MAP?

196
00:13:02,000 --> 00:13:04,000
HOW DID YOU GUESS?

197
00:13:04,000 --> 00:13:06,000
I KNOW HUMAN
NATURE WHERE
TREASURE'S CONCERNED.

198
00:13:06,000 --> 00:13:08,000
WHERE'S THE HARM?
I RETURNED IT.

199
00:13:08,000 --> 00:13:10,000
AFTER TAKING A COPY.

200
00:13:10,000 --> 00:13:12,000
WILL YOU BE
SENDING THE MAP
TO HIS FOLKS?

201
00:13:12,000 --> 00:13:15,000
AND PROVOKE
SOMEBODY ELSE
TO LOSE HIS LIFE?

202
00:13:15,000 --> 00:13:17,000
BESIDES, HE HAS NO FOLKS.

203
00:13:17,000 --> 00:13:19,000
HAVE YOU LOOKED OVER IT?
DO YOU THINK IT'S GENUINE?

204
00:13:19,000 --> 00:13:22,000
IT'S UNEXPLORED COUNTRY.
NOBODY KNOWS.

205
00:13:22,000 --> 00:13:25,000
YOU'RE LOOKING AT A MAN
WHO MEANS TO KNOW.

206
00:13:25,000 --> 00:13:26,000
YOU'RE NOT GONNA
TAKE THAT GIRL--

207
00:13:26,000 --> 00:13:28,000
WHAT DO YOU
TAKE ME FOR?

208
00:13:28,000 --> 00:13:32,000
I'M HER FATHER,
NOT A MURDERER.
I SHALL GO ALONE.

209
00:13:32,000 --> 00:13:35,000
IN ALL ME LIFE, I MAY
NEVER GET ANOTHER
CHANCE LIKE THIS.

210
00:13:35,000 --> 00:13:36,000
OF DYING?

211
00:13:36,000 --> 00:13:39,000
OF FINDING AN EXCUSE
FOR HAVING BEEN BORN.

212
00:13:39,000 --> 00:13:43,000
YOU'LL THINK ME A CASUAL
KIND OF A MICK, WHO
DOESN'T CARE A CRUST

213
00:13:43,000 --> 00:13:47,000
IF I'VE A SHILLING IN ME
POCKET TO BUY A MEAL FOR ME
OWN FLESH AND BLOOD,

214
00:13:47,000 --> 00:13:49,000
BUT IT'S THE WAY
WE IRISH ARE,

215
00:13:49,000 --> 00:13:52,000
TO TAKE OUR TROUBLES
WITH A SMILE IN OUR TEETH

216
00:13:52,000 --> 00:13:55,000
WHILE UNDERNEATH,
THERE IS DEEP SHAME
IN ME HEART.

217
00:13:55,000 --> 00:13:59,000
DO YOU THINK I DON'T KNOW
WHAT I OWE TO THAT CHILD
ASLEEP THERE?

218
00:13:59,000 --> 00:14:03,000
I DO KNOW AND HERE
IS WHERE I MEAN TO PAY
THAT DEBT IN FULL.

219
00:14:03,000 --> 00:14:05,000
WITH YOUR LIFE, HUH?

220
00:14:05,000 --> 00:14:06,000
IF GOD WILLS IT,
WITH ME LIFE.

221
00:14:06,000 --> 00:14:09,000
HOW DO YOU PROPOSE
TO MAKE THE JOURNEY?

222
00:14:09,000 --> 00:14:11,000
HASN'T PROVIDENCE
SENT ME A TEAM OF OXEN?

223
00:14:11,000 --> 00:14:16,000
AND A WAGON, AND STRENGTH
AND PURPOSE TO CARRY ME
TO THE ENDS OF THE EARTH?

224
00:14:16,000 --> 00:14:17,000
YOU KNOW, O'BRIEN,

225
00:14:17,000 --> 00:14:20,000
THERE'S ONLY ONE KIND OF MAN
THAT IS USELESS TO ARGUE WITH.

226
00:14:20,000 --> 00:14:22,000
AND THAT IS?

227
00:14:22,000 --> 00:14:23,000
A FOOL.

228
00:14:23,000 --> 00:14:27,000
EH.

229
00:14:27,000 --> 00:14:32,000
[Men speaking Kukuana]

230
00:14:34,000 --> 00:14:39,000
INKOOSI,  OUR WAGON,
WHERE IS IT?

231
00:14:44,000 --> 00:14:47,000
I'LL TAKE YOU ON.
AT LEAST YOU'LL BE SURE
OF FOOD AND A WAGE.

232
00:14:47,000 --> 00:14:49,000
KATHY, WAKE UP!

233
00:14:49,000 --> 00:14:54,000
I DO NOT WORK FOR
MONEY AND YOU DO
NOT GO MY WAY.

234
00:14:57,000 --> 00:14:58,000
[Quartermain]
KATHY!

235
00:14:58,000 --> 00:15:03,000
ALL RIGHT.

236
00:15:10,000 --> 00:15:13,000
ALLAN QUARTERMAIN,
HE'S GONE AFTER
THE TREASURE.

237
00:15:13,000 --> 00:15:14,000
I KNOW.

238
00:15:14,000 --> 00:15:15,000
WITHOUT ME.

239
00:15:15,000 --> 00:15:17,000
ME, WHO LAY DREAMING
OF THE WAY WE'D GO TOGETHER.

240
00:15:17,000 --> 00:15:19,000
DID YOU EVER HEAR
OF SUCH A THING?

241
00:15:19,000 --> 00:15:21,000
[Quartermain]
HURRY UP,
THEY'RE STARTING.

242
00:15:21,000 --> 00:15:23,000
YOU'RE HEADING THE WRONG WAY.

243
00:15:23,000 --> 00:15:24,000
AREN'T WE GOING
AFTER ME FATHER?

244
00:15:24,000 --> 00:15:26,000
NO.
BUT--

245
00:15:26,000 --> 00:15:27,000
PUT ON YOUR BOOTS
AND GET INTO THE WAGON.

246
00:15:27,000 --> 00:15:29,000
I TOLD YOUR FATHER
I'D LOOK AFTER YOU.

247
00:15:29,000 --> 00:15:33,000
YOU KNEW HE WAS GOING
AND YOU LET HIM GO BY HIMSELF.

248
00:15:33,000 --> 00:15:36,000
ALLAN QUARTERMAIN,
WILL YOU TAKE ME AFTER
ME FATHER, PLEASE?

249
00:15:36,000 --> 00:15:38,000
WE'LL LOOK FOR
THE MINES TOGETHER.

250
00:15:38,000 --> 00:15:41,000
AND WHEN WE FIND THEM,
YOU'LL HAVE YOUR SHARE

251
00:15:41,000 --> 00:15:44,000
AND MORE, MUCH MORE.

252
00:15:44,000 --> 00:15:47,000
DOESN'T A FORTUNE
MEAN ANYTHING TO YOU?

253
00:15:47,000 --> 00:15:52,000
ALL RIGHT, IF YOU WON'T
TAKE ME IN YOUR WAGON
I'LL GO ON ME OWN 2 FEET.

254
00:15:56,000 --> 00:15:58,000
DID YOU HEAR WHAT I SAID?

255
00:15:58,000 --> 00:16:00,000
I DID.

256
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:02,000
THEN WHY DON'T YOU
SAY SOMETHING?

257
00:16:02,000 --> 00:16:06,000
[Quartermain]
BECAUSE YOU'RE
NOT GOING TO DO IT.

258
00:16:06,000 --> 00:16:08,000
THE  INKOOSIKAS  GOES
ACROSS THE RIVER.

259
00:16:08,000 --> 00:16:09,000
YES, I DO.

260
00:16:09,000 --> 00:16:11,000
WHAT BUSINESS IS IT
OF YOURS?

261
00:16:11,000 --> 00:16:13,000
THE  INKOOSIKAS  HAS
THE MAP. I GUIDE HER.

262
00:16:13,000 --> 00:16:15,000
THE MAP'S IN MY WAGON.
NO ONE'S GOING
ACROSS THE RIVER.

263
00:16:15,000 --> 00:16:18,000
KATHY, GET INTO
THAT WAGON.

264
00:16:18,000 --> 00:16:21,000
GET INTO THAT WAGON!

265
00:16:21,000 --> 00:16:23,000
WHAT'S YOUR NAME?

266
00:16:23,000 --> 00:16:24,000
I HAVE MANY NAMES.

267
00:16:24,000 --> 00:16:25,000
ONE'LL DO.
UMBOPA.

268
00:16:25,000 --> 00:16:28,000
WHERE DO YOU COME FROM?

269
00:16:28,000 --> 00:16:29,000
YOU'RE AFTER
DIAMONDS.

270
00:16:29,000 --> 00:16:31,000
WHITE MEN CARE
FOR DIAMONDS.

271
00:16:31,000 --> 00:16:34,000
THEN WHY DO YOU
WANT TO GO NORTH?
MOVE UP.

272
00:16:34,000 --> 00:16:36,000
[Speaking Kukuana]

273
00:16:36,000 --> 00:16:38,000
NOW, LOOK HERE, UMBOPA.

274
00:16:38,000 --> 00:16:41,000
IF YOU WON'T TAKE SERVICE
WITH ME, I DON'T WANT YOU
HANGING ABOUT MY CAMPS.

275
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:46,000
[Speaking Kukuana]

276
00:16:51,000 --> 00:16:53,000
THAT FELLA'S
UP TO NO GOOD.

277
00:16:53,000 --> 00:16:58,000
ALLAN QUARTERMAIN,
I'LL NEVER SPEAK
TO YOU AGAIN. NEVER!

278
00:16:59,000 --> 00:17:04,000
I'M USED TO SILENCE.

279
00:17:58,000 --> 00:18:02,000
[Shouting]

280
00:18:02,000 --> 00:18:04,000
[Man speaking
Kukuana]

281
00:18:04,000 --> 00:18:07,000
[Quartermain
speaking Kukuana]

282
00:18:07,000 --> 00:18:08,000
MY CLIENTS ARRIVED
LAST NIGHT.

283
00:18:08,000 --> 00:18:11,000
IT'LL BE QUITE NICE
TO HAVE SOMEBODY
TO TALK TO.

284
00:18:11,000 --> 00:18:15,000
PUT THE ENGLISHMEN'S
GEAR IN HERE. WE'LL
USE THIS WAGON.

285
00:18:15,000 --> 00:18:17,000
HOW ARE YOU,
QUARTERMAIN?

286
00:18:17,000 --> 00:18:19,000
HOW ARE YOU, SIR?
I'M AFRAID I KEPT
YOU WAITING.

287
00:18:19,000 --> 00:18:21,000
THIS IS
MISS O'BRIEN.

288
00:18:21,000 --> 00:18:23,000
[Henry]
HOW DO YOU DO?

289
00:18:23,000 --> 00:18:25,000
DID YOU HAVE
A GOOD TREK?

290
00:18:25,000 --> 00:18:28,000
NO, I DID NOT.

291
00:18:28,000 --> 00:18:32,000
DON'T MIND MISS
O'BRIEN, SIR HENRY.
SHE'S STRONG AND SILENT.

292
00:18:32,000 --> 00:18:34,000
THE MAP IS
IN THE WAGON.

293
00:18:34,000 --> 00:18:36,000
HOW DID YOU
GET HERE?

294
00:18:36,000 --> 00:18:41,000
INKOOSIKAS  DOES NOT
FORGET HER PURPOSE?

295
00:18:48,000 --> 00:18:50,000
GOOD WILL INSISTS
ON HAVING HIS BATH.

296
00:18:50,000 --> 00:18:53,000
NO REASON FOR
BEING UNSANITARY,
EVEN IN AFRICA.

297
00:18:53,000 --> 00:18:56,000
QUITE RIGHT.
WELL, I'LL SEE YOU
BOTH AT DINNER.

298
00:18:56,000 --> 00:18:58,000
YES. HOW DO YOU GET
OUT OF THIS THING?

299
00:18:58,000 --> 00:19:01,000
YOU BETTER ASK
SIR HENRY TO
TIP YOU OUT.

300
00:19:01,000 --> 00:19:02,000
RIGHT.

301
00:19:02,000 --> 00:19:06,000
NO, NO--
[Mumbling]

302
00:19:06,000 --> 00:19:10,000
SIR HENRY.
SIR HENRY CURTIS.

303
00:19:10,000 --> 00:19:12,000
SIR HENRY CURTIS.

304
00:19:12,000 --> 00:19:15,000
WILL YOU HELP ME, PLEASE?
I'M IN TERRIBLE TROUBLE.

305
00:19:15,000 --> 00:19:17,000
MR. QUARTERMAIN WANTS ME
TO SEND THE WAGON NORTH

306
00:19:17,000 --> 00:19:21,000
SO THAT THE BOYS CAN HAVE
CAMP READY WHEN YOU ARRIVE
BUT THEY WON'T OBEY ME.

307
00:19:21,000 --> 00:19:24,000
MUTINY, EH?

308
00:19:24,000 --> 00:19:27,000
GLORY BE TO GOD,
I THOUGHT IT WAS A PIG.

309
00:19:27,000 --> 00:19:28,000
COMMANDER GOOD,
ROYAL NAVY.

310
00:19:28,000 --> 00:19:30,000
RETIRED.

311
00:19:30,000 --> 00:19:31,000
I'LL GO FETCH
QUARTERMAIN.

312
00:19:31,000 --> 00:19:32,000
AH, NO.
PLEASE DON'T.

313
00:19:32,000 --> 00:19:34,000
I DON'T WANT HIM TO
KNOW I'VE HAD TROUBLE.

314
00:19:34,000 --> 00:19:35,000
WILL YOU
SPEAK TO THEM?

315
00:19:35,000 --> 00:19:37,000
OF COURSE I'LL
SPEAK TO THEM.

316
00:19:37,000 --> 00:19:39,000
BY THE WAY,
I THOUGHT YOU WERE
STRONG AND SILENT.

317
00:19:39,000 --> 00:19:44,000
YOU WOULDN'T BELIEVE
MR. QUARTERMAIN.
HE'S A TERRIBLE LIAR.

318
00:19:44,000 --> 00:19:49,000
GENTLEMEN, THE QUEEN.
GOD BLESS HER.

319
00:19:50,000 --> 00:19:52,000
WITH YOUR PERMISSION,
I'LL LIGHT UP.

320
00:19:52,000 --> 00:19:55,000
AND WITH YOURS
I'LL RUN OVER A FEW
OF MY PROPOSALS.

321
00:19:55,000 --> 00:19:59,000
I TAKE IT YOU WANT
TO GET A SABLE
ANTELOPE, SIR HENRY.

322
00:19:59,000 --> 00:20:01,000
IS MISS O'BRIEN OFTEN
AS LATE AS THIS?

323
00:20:01,000 --> 00:20:03,000
SHE'LL SHOW UP
WHEN SHE'S HUNGRY.

324
00:20:03,000 --> 00:20:05,000
SHE SEEMED TO ME
TO BE A CAPABLE
YOUNG PERSON.

325
00:20:05,000 --> 00:20:08,000
HMM--YES, CAPABLE
OF ANYTHING.

326
00:20:08,000 --> 00:20:12,000
SHE'D HAVE STOLEN ONE
OF MY WAGONS IF I HADN'T
KEPT ME EYES OPEN.

327
00:20:12,000 --> 00:20:15,000
[Quartermain]
ANYTHING WRONG?

328
00:20:15,000 --> 00:20:17,000
I TAKE IT IT'S IN ORDER
FOR SIR HENRY TO TELL

329
00:20:17,000 --> 00:20:20,000
YOUR WAGON BOYS TO
OBEY THE YOUNG LADY.

330
00:20:20,000 --> 00:20:23,000
WITH THE RESULT THAT
YOUR WAGON IS NOW
PROCEEDING NORTH

331
00:20:23,000 --> 00:20:26,000
TO ESTABLISH
A CAMP.

332
00:20:26,000 --> 00:20:27,000
BUT SHE TOLD ME--

333
00:20:27,000 --> 00:20:30,000
MY BOY, I'M AFRAID
YOU'RE THE VICTIM
OF A WOMAN'S WILES.

334
00:20:30,000 --> 00:20:31,000
WE MUST GO
AFTER HER.

335
00:20:31,000 --> 00:20:34,000
WE CERTAINLY MUST.
MY ONLY TOOTHBRUSH
IS IN THAT WAGON.

336
00:20:34,000 --> 00:20:37,000
SHE HAS 3 HOURS START.
IT'LL BE 2 DAYS BEFORE
I GATHER A TEAM.

337
00:20:37,000 --> 00:20:40,000
SHE TOLD ME THOSE BOYS
WERE MUTINOUS.

338
00:20:40,000 --> 00:20:44,000
I'M AFRAID, SIR HENRY,
THAT IT'S MISS O'BRIEN
WHO IS MUTINOUS.

339
00:20:44,000 --> 00:20:49,000
WILL YOU HAVE A
LITTLE MORE PORT?

340
00:21:07,000 --> 00:21:10,000
♪ I'M NOT AFRAID

341
00:21:10,000 --> 00:21:12,000
♪ I'M NOT AFRAID

342
00:21:12,000 --> 00:21:16,000
♪ WHY SHOULD I CARE
IF MY JOURNEY'S LONG ♪

343
00:21:16,000 --> 00:21:18,000
♪ I'M SURE TO GET THERE

344
00:21:18,000 --> 00:21:21,000
♪ THOUGH MY JOURNEY'S LONG

345
00:21:21,000 --> 00:21:25,000
♪ MY TEAM AND MY WAGON
ARE STRONG ♪

346
00:21:25,000 --> 00:21:27,000
♪[Playing harmonica]

347
00:21:27,000 --> 00:21:30,000
♪ STRUGGLE ALONG

348
00:21:30,000 --> 00:21:32,000
♪ STRUGGLE ALONG

349
00:21:32,000 --> 00:21:33,000
♪ OXEN OF MINE

350
00:21:33,000 --> 00:21:35,000
♪ TILL YOUR SHOULDERS CRACK

351
00:21:35,000 --> 00:21:37,000
♪ KEEP PLODDING ALONG

352
00:21:37,000 --> 00:21:41,000
♪ TILL YOUR SHOULDERS CRACK

353
00:21:41,000 --> 00:21:46,000
♪ I'LL NEVER BE
TURNING YOU BACK ♪

354
00:21:52,000 --> 00:21:54,000
♪ WALK, WALK

355
00:21:54,000 --> 00:21:56,000
♪ OXEN OF MINE

356
00:21:56,000 --> 00:22:00,000
♪ ANSWER MY WHIP
WHEN IT FALLS ♪

357
00:22:00,000 --> 00:22:02,000
♪ WALK, WALK

358
00:22:02,000 --> 00:22:04,000
♪ KEEP IN YOUR LINE

359
00:22:04,000 --> 00:22:07,000
♪ LEOPARDS WAIT TO GET
THE ONE THAT FALLS ♪

360
00:22:07,000 --> 00:22:09,000
♪ GET UP AND WALK

361
00:22:09,000 --> 00:22:12,000
♪ WALK, OXEN OF MINE

362
00:22:12,000 --> 00:22:16,000
♪ SHINING AS BRIGHT
AS THE MOON ♪

363
00:22:16,000 --> 00:22:18,000
♪ WALK, WALK

364
00:22:18,000 --> 00:22:20,000
♪ KEEP IN YOUR LINE

365
00:22:20,000 --> 00:22:23,000
♪ THERE WILL BE
A WATER HOLE SOON ♪

366
00:22:23,000 --> 00:22:28,000
♪ WE'LL COME TO
THAT WATER HOLE SOON ♪

367
00:22:28,000 --> 00:22:30,000
♪ WALK, WALK

368
00:22:30,000 --> 00:22:32,000
♪ YOU BETTER KEEP ON

369
00:22:32,000 --> 00:22:36,000
♪ THINK OF THAT SUN
IN THE SKY ♪

370
00:22:36,000 --> 00:22:38,000
♪ WALK, WALK

371
00:22:38,000 --> 00:22:40,000
♪ HURRY ALONG

372
00:22:40,000 --> 00:22:43,000
♪ OR THE SUN WILL DRINK
THAT WATER DRY ♪

373
00:22:43,000 --> 00:22:46,000
♪ GET UP AND WALK, WALK

374
00:22:46,000 --> 00:22:48,000
♪ STRAIN AT YOUR LOAD

375
00:22:48,000 --> 00:22:52,000
♪ THOUGH YOU ARE
WEARY AND SORE ♪

376
00:22:52,000 --> 00:22:54,000
♪ WALK, WALK

377
00:22:54,000 --> 00:22:55,000
♪ KEEP TO THE ROAD

378
00:22:55,000 --> 00:23:00,000
♪ SOON YOU'LL BE
RESTING ONCE MORE ♪

379
00:23:00,000 --> 00:23:04,000
♪ SOON YOU'LL BE
RESTING ONCE MORE ♪

380
00:23:04,000 --> 00:23:06,000
♪ WALK, WALK

381
00:23:06,000 --> 00:23:07,000
♪ OXEN OF MINE

382
00:23:07,000 --> 00:23:12,000
♪ ANSWER MY WHIP
WHEN IT FALLS ♪

383
00:23:12,000 --> 00:23:14,000
♪ YAH, YAH

384
00:23:14,000 --> 00:23:16,000
♪ KEEP IN YOUR LINE

385
00:23:16,000 --> 00:23:20,000
♪ LEOPARDS WAIT TO GET
THE ONE THAT FALLS ♪

386
00:23:20,000 --> 00:23:22,000
♪ GET UP YAH, YAH

387
00:23:22,000 --> 00:23:24,000
♪ OXEN OF MINE

388
00:23:24,000 --> 00:23:28,000
♪ SHINING AS BRIGHT
AS THE MOON ♪

389
00:23:28,000 --> 00:23:30,000
♪ YAH, YAH

390
00:23:30,000 --> 00:23:32,000
♪ KEEP IN YOUR LINE

391
00:23:32,000 --> 00:23:36,000
♪ THERE WILL BE
A WATER HOLE SOON ♪

392
00:23:36,000 --> 00:23:41,000
♪ WE'LL COME TO
THAT WATER HOLE SOON ♪

393
00:23:41,000 --> 00:23:43,000
♪ LA-DA-DA-DA

394
00:23:43,000 --> 00:23:46,000
♪ LA-DA-DA-DA

395
00:23:46,000 --> 00:23:50,000
♪ LA-DA-DA-DA
DA-DA-DA-DA-DA ♪

396
00:23:50,000 --> 00:23:53,000
♪ DA-DA-DA-DA

397
00:23:53,000 --> 00:23:58,000
♪ DA-DA

398
00:24:09,000 --> 00:24:12,000
[Quartermain] YOU'RE 9
MILES NORTH OF THE HILL,
HEADING FOR THE DESERT,

399
00:24:12,000 --> 00:24:13,000
IN A STOLEN
WAGON.

400
00:24:13,000 --> 00:24:16,000
AND WHAT'S LEFT
OF MY TROUSERS.

401
00:24:16,000 --> 00:24:17,000
[Quartermain]
YOU'RE COMING
BACK TOMORROW.

402
00:24:17,000 --> 00:24:20,000
MEANWHILE, COMMANDER
GOOD WOULD LIKE
HIS TOOTHBRUSH.

403
00:24:20,000 --> 00:24:24,000
YES.

404
00:24:24,000 --> 00:24:28,000
IF YOU WEREN'T A GIRL,
I'D GIVE YOU THE
HIDING OF YOUR LIFE.

405
00:24:28,000 --> 00:24:33,000
ASHAMED OF YOURSELF?

406
00:24:36,000 --> 00:24:41,000
BUT I'D DO IT AGAIN.

407
00:24:50,000 --> 00:24:51,000
READY TO
COME BACK?

408
00:24:51,000 --> 00:24:52,000
I'M NOT
COMING BACK.

409
00:24:52,000 --> 00:24:55,000
I MADE UP ME MIND
TO GO AFTER ME FATHER
AND I'M GOING.

410
00:24:55,000 --> 00:24:56,000
NOT IN MY WAGON.

411
00:24:56,000 --> 00:24:58,000
I DON'T WANT YOUR
WAGON ANYMORE.

412
00:24:58,000 --> 00:25:01,000
YOU CAN'T TAKE A WAGON
OVER THE DESERT BECAUSE
YOU CAN'T TAKE ANY OXEN.

413
00:25:01,000 --> 00:25:02,000
WHY?

414
00:25:02,000 --> 00:25:04,000
BECAUSE THEY
DRINK TOO MUCH.

415
00:25:04,000 --> 00:25:05,000
WHO TOLD YOU THAT?

416
00:25:05,000 --> 00:25:09,000
I DID,  INKOOSI.

417
00:25:09,000 --> 00:25:10,000
WHAT ARE YOU
DOING HERE?

418
00:25:10,000 --> 00:25:12,000
[Kathy]
I BROUGHT HIM.

419
00:25:12,000 --> 00:25:15,000
LOOK, KATHY, I DON'T KNOW
WHAT THIS MAN'S
BEEN TELLING YOU,

420
00:25:15,000 --> 00:25:18,000
BUT I GIVE YOU
MY WORD NO ONE CAN
CROSS THAT DESERT.

421
00:25:18,000 --> 00:25:20,000
HOW DOES
THE  INKOOSI  KNOW?

422
00:25:20,000 --> 00:25:22,000
I'M GONNA TRY.
I'M NOT AFRAID.

423
00:25:22,000 --> 00:25:23,000
THE  INKOOSIKAS
IS READY.

424
00:25:23,000 --> 00:25:28,000
I'M IN CHARGE
HERE. CLEAR OUT!

425
00:25:28,000 --> 00:25:30,000
WAIT, WE CAN'T
LET THESE 2
GO ALONE,

426
00:25:30,000 --> 00:25:32,000
BUT WHY
SHOULDN'T WE
GO WITH THEM?

427
00:25:32,000 --> 00:25:33,000
GOOD SUGGESTION.
SOLVES THE PROBLEM.

428
00:25:33,000 --> 00:25:35,000
I WON'T HAVE IT.

429
00:25:35,000 --> 00:25:36,000
NOBODY'S ASKING YOU.

430
00:25:36,000 --> 00:25:38,000
I THOUGHT YOU WANTED
TO GO HUNTING.

431
00:25:38,000 --> 00:25:43,000
YOU KNOW, HUNTING,
FISHING, ANYTHING WITH A
LITTLE ADVENTURE IN IT.

432
00:25:43,000 --> 00:25:47,000
DO YOU KNOW HOW MEN
DIE FOR LACK OF WATER?

433
00:25:47,000 --> 00:25:51,000
THIRST, BURNING THIRST
THAT TURNS TO PAIN.

434
00:25:51,000 --> 00:25:55,000
TORTURE, THEN
YOU GO MAD

435
00:25:55,000 --> 00:25:58,000
AND THE SUN
KILLS YOU.

436
00:25:58,000 --> 00:26:00,000
IMAGINATIVE
FELLOW, ISN'T HE?

437
00:26:00,000 --> 00:26:02,000
QUARTERMAIN.

438
00:26:02,000 --> 00:26:05,000
I'M SORRY OUR TRIP'S
HAD TO END LIKE THIS.

439
00:26:05,000 --> 00:26:06,000
HOW DO YOU
MEAN "END"?

440
00:26:06,000 --> 00:26:08,000
WE'LL BE AWAY
FOR SOME TIME.

441
00:26:08,000 --> 00:26:12,000
CAN'T ASK YOU
TO WAIT FOR US.

442
00:26:12,000 --> 00:26:14,000
SIR HENRY CURTIS,

443
00:26:14,000 --> 00:26:16,000
I WAS ENGAGED TO
TAKE YOU UPCOUNTRY

444
00:26:16,000 --> 00:26:19,000
AND TO BRING YOU
BACK TO THE BEST
OF MY ABILITY.

445
00:26:19,000 --> 00:26:23,000
I HAPPEN TO BE A
MAN WHO RESPECTS
A CONTRACT.

446
00:26:23,000 --> 00:26:25,000
I'M LINING
UP WITH THE
REST OF YOU.

447
00:26:25,000 --> 00:26:29,000
YOU'RE A GOOD
FELLOW, QUARTERMAIN.

448
00:26:29,000 --> 00:26:34,000
ON THE CONTRARY,
I'M A FOOL.

449
00:27:25,000 --> 00:27:28,000
HOW ARE YOUR FEET?

450
00:27:28,000 --> 00:27:31,000
ALL RIGHT.
HOW ARE YOURS?

451
00:27:31,000 --> 00:27:34,000
FINE.

452
00:27:34,000 --> 00:27:39,000
NICE ABOUT OUR FEET,
ISN'T IT?

453
00:27:41,000 --> 00:27:44,000
ARE YOU REALLY GOING
ALL THROUGH THIS
JUST FOR DIAMONDS?

454
00:27:44,000 --> 00:27:45,000
THE  INKOOSI
SAYS SO.

455
00:27:45,000 --> 00:27:47,000
I DIDN'T SAY ANYTHING.
I'M ASKING YOU.

456
00:27:47,000 --> 00:27:48,000
WHY IS
INKOOSI  GOING?

457
00:27:48,000 --> 00:27:51,000
BLESSED IF
I KNOW.

458
00:27:51,000 --> 00:27:56,000
YOU'RE NOT ONE
FOR A BIT OF
GOSSIP, ARE YOU?

459
00:28:39,000 --> 00:28:44,000
THE MOUNTAINS DON'T
SEEM TO GET ANY
NEARER, DO THEY?

460
00:28:44,000 --> 00:28:46,000
NO, THEY DON'T,
DO THEY?

461
00:28:46,000 --> 00:28:48,000
NO--NO, THEY--

462
00:28:48,000 --> 00:28:51,000
NO, THEY DON'T.

463
00:28:51,000 --> 00:28:53,000
FEELING BETTER?

464
00:28:53,000 --> 00:28:55,000
MUST YOU KEEP
ON ASKING ME?

465
00:28:55,000 --> 00:28:56,000
I NEEDN'T.

466
00:28:56,000 --> 00:29:01,000
I'D SURE MISS IT
IF YOU DIDN'T.

467
00:29:01,000 --> 00:29:03,000
HOW LONG WILL
THE WATER LAST?

468
00:29:03,000 --> 00:29:05,000
TOMORROW.

469
00:29:05,000 --> 00:29:07,000
IF I--

470
00:29:07,000 --> 00:29:09,000
IF I DON'T GET
ANOTHER CHANCE,

471
00:29:09,000 --> 00:29:14,000
I'M SORRY ABOUT
EVERYTHING.

472
00:29:33,000 --> 00:29:34,000
WHAT ARE THOSE
BIRDS UP THERE?

473
00:29:34,000 --> 00:29:37,000
[Umbopa]
ASSVOGELS.

474
00:29:37,000 --> 00:29:39,000
THEY MUST BE TO LIVE
IN A PLACE LIKE THIS.

475
00:29:39,000 --> 00:29:42,000
WE CALL THEM
"THE BIRD THAT
SMELLS DEATH."

476
00:29:42,000 --> 00:29:47,000
HUH? OH.

477
00:29:57,000 --> 00:30:01,000
GOOD! COME HERE.

478
00:30:01,000 --> 00:30:04,000
O'BRIEN'S WAGON.

479
00:30:04,000 --> 00:30:09,000
GO BACK AND
KEEP HER TALKING.

480
00:30:24,000 --> 00:30:29,000
FETCH THE OTHERS.

481
00:30:39,000 --> 00:30:42,000
[Henry]
THAT'S THE LAST
RATION OF WATER.

482
00:30:42,000 --> 00:30:47,000
HALF A BOTTLE EACH.

483
00:30:53,000 --> 00:30:56,000
THAT'S GOOD, I--

484
00:30:56,000 --> 00:31:01,000
I SEE BY THE MAP THAT
WE OUGHT TO GET TO PAN BAD
WATER BY MIDDAY TOMORROW.

485
00:31:03,000 --> 00:31:06,000
WHY'S IT CALLED
"PAN BAD WATER"?

486
00:31:06,000 --> 00:31:08,000
BECAUSE IN 300 YEARS
IT MAY HAVE DRIED UP.

487
00:31:08,000 --> 00:31:10,000
OH...

488
00:31:10,000 --> 00:31:15,000
OH, I SEE, YES.

489
00:31:34,000 --> 00:31:38,000
GO ON,
DRINK IT.

490
00:31:38,000 --> 00:31:40,000
WHAT'S THE
USE, CURTIS?

491
00:31:40,000 --> 00:31:45,000
THERE'S NO POINT
IN HER SURVIVING US.

492
00:31:56,000 --> 00:32:00,000
SAND! GO DOWN!

493
00:32:00,000 --> 00:32:03,000
RUN!

494
00:32:03,000 --> 00:32:08,000
[Wind whistling]

495
00:32:13,000 --> 00:32:18,000
[Wind howling]

496
00:32:35,000 --> 00:32:38,000
I SMELL WATER.

497
00:32:38,000 --> 00:32:40,000
I SMELL WATER.

498
00:32:40,000 --> 00:32:43,000
I SMELL WATER.

499
00:32:43,000 --> 00:32:47,000
[Speaking Kukuana]

500
00:32:47,000 --> 00:32:52,000
[Shouting]

501
00:32:55,000 --> 00:33:00,000
[Speaking Kukuana]

502
00:33:19,000 --> 00:33:24,000
LOOK! THE MOUNTAINS
ARE NEAR!

503
00:33:40,000 --> 00:33:43,000
[Umbopa]
♪ CLIMBING UP
CLIMBING UP ♪

504
00:33:43,000 --> 00:33:48,000
