539
00:36:36,000 --> 00:36:41,000
♪ MIGHTY MOUNTAIN

540
00:37:11,000 --> 00:37:12,000
BREAKFAST READY?

541
00:37:12,000 --> 00:37:14,000
[Kathy]
NEARLY.

542
00:37:14,000 --> 00:37:16,000
WE HAD MELONS FOR
BREAKFAST YESTERDAY.

543
00:37:16,000 --> 00:37:19,000
WE DID.

544
00:37:19,000 --> 00:37:20,000
AND MELONS
THE DAY BEFORE.

545
00:37:20,000 --> 00:37:22,000
WE DID.

546
00:37:22,000 --> 00:37:24,000
I SUPPOSE WE'RE GONNA
HAVE MELONS TODAY?

547
00:37:24,000 --> 00:37:26,000
[Both]
WE ARE.

548
00:37:26,000 --> 00:37:31,000
DON'T THE BIRDS
IN THIS COUNTRY
EVER LAY EGGS?

549
00:37:36,000 --> 00:37:41,000
I WONDER HOW
FAR ME FATHER
IS AHEAD OF US?

550
00:37:41,000 --> 00:37:43,000
YOU SURE HE
GOT THIS FAR?

551
00:37:43,000 --> 00:37:45,000
OF COURSE I AM.

552
00:37:45,000 --> 00:37:50,000
PATRICK O'BRIEN HAS
ALWAYS DONE WHAT HE
SET HIS MIND TO.

553
00:37:54,000 --> 00:37:57,000
WHAT DID YOU THINK
ABOUT IN THE DESERT?

554
00:37:57,000 --> 00:38:00,000
SAND, MOSTLY.

555
00:38:00,000 --> 00:38:01,000
DID YOU EVER
THINK OF ME?

556
00:38:01,000 --> 00:38:04,000
YES...

557
00:38:04,000 --> 00:38:06,000
YOU AND
THE SAND.

558
00:38:06,000 --> 00:38:10,000
I'M GLAD OF THAT BECAUSE
YOU'RE GONNA SEE A LOT OF
ME IN THE NEXT FEW WEEKS.

559
00:38:10,000 --> 00:38:12,000
AM I?

560
00:38:12,000 --> 00:38:13,000
I'M AFRAID YOU
CAN'T AVOID IT.

561
00:38:13,000 --> 00:38:18,000
YOU SEE, WE'RE IN
UNINHABITED COUNTRY.

562
00:38:18,000 --> 00:38:20,000
I HATE TO CONTRADICT
YOU BUT,

563
00:38:20,000 --> 00:38:25,000
THERE'S A MAN
BEHIND THAT ROCK--

564
00:38:27,000 --> 00:38:32,000
SEVERAL MEN.

565
00:38:36,000 --> 00:38:37,000
THEY SEEM ANXIOUS
TO MEET US.

566
00:38:37,000 --> 00:38:42,000
MUCH TOO ANXIOUS.

567
00:38:48,000 --> 00:38:53,000
[Shouting in Kukuana]

568
00:39:04,000 --> 00:39:06,000
WHAT'S HAPPENED?

569
00:39:06,000 --> 00:39:09,000
THEY SAY, "WHAT MANNER
OF MAN IS THIS WITH THE
BEAUTIFUL WHITE LEGS,

570
00:39:09,000 --> 00:39:12,000
"WHO GROWS HAIR ON
ONE SIDE OF HIS FACE

571
00:39:12,000 --> 00:39:17,000
"AND CAN PLUCK HIS EYE
FROM HIS HEAD AND REPLACE
IT WHERE IT GROWS?"

572
00:39:23,000 --> 00:39:28,000
[Speaking Kukuana]

573
00:39:28,000 --> 00:39:31,000
HE'S TELLING THEM YOU ARE
WHITE GODS FROM THE SKIES.

574
00:39:31,000 --> 00:39:36,000
YOU MEAN, ON ACCOUNT
OF MY LEGS?

575
00:39:36,000 --> 00:39:39,000
I NEVER THOUGHT
THEY WERE AS GOOD
AS ALL THAT.

576
00:39:39,000 --> 00:39:44,000
[Speaking Kukuana]

577
00:39:54,000 --> 00:39:59,000
HE COULDN'T HAVE DONE
THAT BETTER IF HE'D
BEEN AN IRISHMAN.

578
00:40:03,000 --> 00:40:08,000
♪[Drum beating]

579
00:40:16,000 --> 00:40:21,000
♪[Drums beating]

580
00:40:35,000 --> 00:40:40,000
♪[Chanting]

581
00:41:09,000 --> 00:41:14,000
[Speaking Kukuana]

582
00:41:25,000 --> 00:41:30,000
[Man shouting]

583
00:41:34,000 --> 00:41:39,000
♪[Chanting, drums beating]

584
00:41:44,000 --> 00:41:47,000
[Shouting in Kukuana]

585
00:41:47,000 --> 00:41:52,000
♪[Chanting and drumming]

586
00:42:23,000 --> 00:42:27,000
THERE ARE A LOT OF
PEOPLE ABOUT FOR
AN UNINHABITED COUNTRY.

587
00:42:27,000 --> 00:42:28,000
[Quartermain]
THIS IS A MILITARY CROWD.

588
00:42:28,000 --> 00:42:29,000
I HOPE THE
COOKING'S GOOD.

589
00:42:29,000 --> 00:42:32,000
THOSE ARE THE
SOLDIERS' QUARTERS.
THAT'S THE KING'S HUT.

590
00:42:32,000 --> 00:42:34,000
BUCKINGHAM PALACE AND
WILLINGTON BARRACKS.

591
00:42:34,000 --> 00:42:39,000
SO UNLIKE THE HOME
LIFE OF OUR DEAR
QUEEN, ISN'T IT?

592
00:42:40,000 --> 00:42:44,000
SUPPOSE PATRICK
O'BRIEN'S IN THERE?

593
00:42:44,000 --> 00:42:46,000
DON'T WORRY.
ME FATHER'S GONE
AFTER DIAMONDS.

594
00:42:46,000 --> 00:42:48,000
KING SOLOMON'S MINES,
THAT'S WHERE
WE'LL FIND HIM.

595
00:42:48,000 --> 00:42:53,000
IF THERE IS
SUCH A MINE.

596
00:42:53,000 --> 00:42:58,000
[Speaking Kukuana]

597
00:42:59,000 --> 00:43:01,000
I SUPPOSE HE SAYS
HE ISN'T IN.

598
00:43:01,000 --> 00:43:03,000
HE SAID, "THE
TWALA,  THE KING

599
00:43:03,000 --> 00:43:08,000
"WILL SEE THE STRANGERS
WHO COME TO HIS LAND
AND CLAIM TO BE GODS."

600
00:43:26,000 --> 00:43:31,000
[Cheering]

601
00:43:38,000 --> 00:43:41,000
I DON'T LIKE THE
LOOK OF THEIR SPEARS.

602
00:43:41,000 --> 00:43:43,000
IT'S ALL RIGHT.
THEY THINK
WE'RE GODS.

603
00:43:43,000 --> 00:43:44,000
I HOPE THE
TWALA  DOES.

604
00:43:44,000 --> 00:43:49,000
HEAD UP. IF HE
THINKS WE'RE AFRAID
ANYTHING MAY HAPPEN.

605
00:43:52,000 --> 00:43:57,000
[Speaking Kukuana]

606
00:44:13,000 --> 00:44:18,000
HA HA HA HA...

607
00:44:20,000 --> 00:44:25,000
[Shouting]

608
00:44:25,000 --> 00:44:30,000
WOULD IT DO ANY GOOD
IF I WHIPPED OFF MY
TROUSERS, DO YOU THINK?

609
00:44:31,000 --> 00:44:34,000
[Speaking Kukuana]

610
00:44:34,000 --> 00:44:37,000
HE ASKS,"WHY DO
THE GODS HONOR
HIS KINGDOM?

611
00:44:37,000 --> 00:44:38,000
"IS IT THE WHITE
STONES THEY SEEK?"

612
00:44:38,000 --> 00:44:39,000
DIAMONDS!

613
00:44:39,000 --> 00:44:41,000
THERE IS A MINE.
TELL HIM YES.

614
00:44:41,000 --> 00:44:44,000
[Speaking Kukuana]

615
00:44:44,000 --> 00:44:46,000
[Speaking Kukuana]

616
00:44:46,000 --> 00:44:47,000
HE'S GONNA
TAKE US.

617
00:44:47,000 --> 00:44:48,000
KING SOLOMON'S
MINES.

618
00:44:48,000 --> 00:44:50,000
THE GREATEST
TREASURE IN
THE WORLD.

619
00:44:50,000 --> 00:44:53,000
WITH ME FATHER
INSIDE FILLING
HIS POCKETS.

620
00:44:53,000 --> 00:44:58,000
[Shouting orders]

621
00:45:03,000 --> 00:45:08,000
[Crowd murmuring]

622
00:45:09,000 --> 00:45:12,000
IT SEEMS THEY
ARE NICE FELLOWS
AFTER ALL.

623
00:45:12,000 --> 00:45:17,000
I HOPE
YOU'RE RIGHT.

624
00:45:31,000 --> 00:45:34,000
WHAT ARE YOU GOING
TO DO WITH YOUR SHARE
OF THE MONEY?

625
00:45:34,000 --> 00:45:39,000
IF WE GET OUT OF THIS,
GO BACK TO ENGLAND
AND KEEP SHEEP.

626
00:45:39,000 --> 00:45:44,000
I THINK I'LL BUY MYSELF
A BATTLESHIP AND
REJOIN THE NAVY.

627
00:45:44,000 --> 00:45:49,000
♪[Chanting]

628
00:45:56,000 --> 00:45:57,000
SCARED?

629
00:45:57,000 --> 00:46:00,000
OF COURSE
I'M NOT.

630
00:46:00,000 --> 00:46:05,000
NOT VERY.

631
00:46:06,000 --> 00:46:09,000
KING SOLOMON'S ROAD
AND THE SILENT
ONES TO GUARD IT,

632
00:46:09,000 --> 00:46:11,000
BROKEN AND
OVERGROWN.

633
00:46:11,000 --> 00:46:14,000
I WONDER HOW MANY
CIVILIZATIONS HAVE
PERISHED LIKE THIS ONE?

634
00:46:14,000 --> 00:46:17,000
SOLOMON HAD
NOTHING TO DO
WITH IDOLS.

635
00:46:17,000 --> 00:46:20,000
THE PHOENICIANS DID.
THEY WERE THE GREAT
TRADERS OF SOLOMON'S TIME.

636
00:46:20,000 --> 00:46:25,000
PERHAPS SOME
PHOENICIAN RAN
THE MINE.

637
00:46:35,000 --> 00:46:39,000
GAGOOL, THE  WITCH
DOCTOR WHO LOOKS
AFTER THE MINES.

638
00:46:39,000 --> 00:46:44,000
THESE PEOPLE
BELIEVE THAT SHE'S
100'S OF YEARS OLD.

639
00:46:50,000 --> 00:46:55,000
WOULD YOU SAY
THAT SHE WAS
WELL-PRESERVED?

640
00:47:04,000 --> 00:47:09,000
REMINDS ME
OF MY POOR OLD
AUNT HANNAH.

641
00:47:10,000 --> 00:47:12,000
SHE CAME TO NO GOOD.

642
00:47:12,000 --> 00:47:16,000
[Speaking Kukuana]

643
00:47:16,000 --> 00:47:19,000
SHE ASKS WHY THE
WHITE MAN'S SERVANT
WALKS LIKE A PRINCE?

644
00:47:19,000 --> 00:47:24,000
I'VE NOTICED IT
MYSELF, AN UNCOMMONLY
GOOD WALKER.

645
00:47:24,000 --> 00:47:28,000
ASK HER IF SHE'S
SEEN A WHITE MAN.

646
00:47:28,000 --> 00:47:33,000
[Speaking Kukuana]

647
00:47:35,000 --> 00:47:40,000
[Speaking Kukuana]

648
00:47:43,000 --> 00:47:44,000
SHE HAS?

649
00:47:44,000 --> 00:47:45,000
PERHAPS IT WAS
YESTERDAY,

650
00:47:45,000 --> 00:47:47,000
PERHAPS IT WAS
100 YEARS AGO.

651
00:47:47,000 --> 00:47:52,000
TIME HAS NO
MEANING TO HER.

652
00:47:54,000 --> 00:47:59,000
[Rumbling]

653
00:48:04,000 --> 00:48:08,000
THROUGH THAT DOOR,
SLAVES BROUGHT JEWELS

654
00:48:08,000 --> 00:48:10,000
FOR THE QUEEN
OF SHEBA THOUSANDS
OF YEARS AGO.

655
00:48:10,000 --> 00:48:15,000
AND PATRICK O'BRIEN
WENT IN TO FIND HIS
FORTUNE. COME ON.

656
00:48:18,000 --> 00:48:22,000
CAREFUL,
INKOOSI.

657
00:48:22,000 --> 00:48:24,000
TWALA DARE NOT HARM
YOU HERE. THE PEOPLE
THINK YOU GODS.

658
00:48:24,000 --> 00:48:27,000
ONCE INSIDE,
HE HAS NO
ONE TO FEAR.

659
00:48:27,000 --> 00:48:29,000
THE STONE
WILL ROLL BACK.

660
00:48:29,000 --> 00:48:32,000
[Shouting]

661
00:48:32,000 --> 00:48:34,000
COME AWAY.

662
00:48:34,000 --> 00:48:39,000
[Speaking Kukuana]

663
00:48:39,000 --> 00:48:42,000
[Shouting]

664
00:48:42,000 --> 00:48:43,000
[Rumbling]

665
00:48:43,000 --> 00:48:48,000
GET OUT OF HERE!

666
00:48:49,000 --> 00:48:50,000
GIVE ME THAT!

667
00:48:50,000 --> 00:48:53,000
[Shouts]

668
00:48:53,000 --> 00:48:54,000
KILL HIM,
YOU'LL HAVE
THE LOT ON US.

669
00:48:54,000 --> 00:48:59,000
THEY'VE NEVER
SEEN A GUN
FIRED BEFORE.

670
00:48:59,000 --> 00:49:04,000
[Crowd screaming]

671
00:49:14,000 --> 00:49:19,000
I BET THAT
MADE HIM FEEL
PRETTY SILLY.

672
00:49:20,000 --> 00:49:25,000
♪[Drums beating]

673
00:49:30,000 --> 00:49:35,000
♪[Chanting]

674
00:49:50,000 --> 00:49:52,000
OUR ONE CHANCE IS
TO ESCAPE BEFORE
THEY MAKE UP THEIR MINDS.

675
00:49:52,000 --> 00:49:54,000
I'M AFRAID IT IS.

676
00:49:54,000 --> 00:49:56,000
SOMEONE WILL
HAVE TO DEAL
WITH THE GUARD.

677
00:49:56,000 --> 00:49:58,000
PITY, SEEMED
A VERY DECENT
FELLOW.

678
00:49:58,000 --> 00:49:59,000
ALL RIGHT, BUT
I'M STOPPING HERE.

679
00:49:59,000 --> 00:50:02,000
KATHY, BE SENSIBLE.
YOU CAN'T.

680
00:50:02,000 --> 00:50:04,000
I CAME HERE
TO FIND ME FATHER.

681
00:50:04,000 --> 00:50:09,000
THERE ISN'T A VESTIGE OF
PROOF THAT YOUR FATHER
EVER REACHED HERE.

682
00:50:10,000 --> 00:50:15,000
HAVE IT YOUR OWN WAY.

683
00:50:15,000 --> 00:50:18,000
ME SHAMROCK!

684
00:50:18,000 --> 00:50:21,000
BUT I--IT'S NOT--

685
00:50:21,000 --> 00:50:22,000
IT IS HIS!
ME FATHER'S!

686
00:50:22,000 --> 00:50:24,000
SO HE IS HERE.

687
00:50:24,000 --> 00:50:28,000
NOW DO YOU WANT
ME TO RUN AWAY?

688
00:50:28,000 --> 00:50:29,000
WHERE DID YOU
FIND THIS?

689
00:50:29,000 --> 00:50:32,000
ON THE WAY
TO THE MINE.

690
00:50:32,000 --> 00:50:35,000
KATHY, YOU SAW WHAT
NEARLY HAPPENED TO US.

691
00:50:35,000 --> 00:50:38,000
THIS PROVES THAT IT
MUST HAVE HAPPENED
TO YOUR FATHER.

692
00:50:38,000 --> 00:50:41,000
IF YOUR FATHER
LOVED YOU AS MUCH
AS YOU LOVE HIM,

693
00:50:41,000 --> 00:50:44,000
HE'D BE THE LAST ONE
TO WANT YOU TO STAY.

694
00:50:44,000 --> 00:50:46,000
WOULDN'T HE?

695
00:50:46,000 --> 00:50:48,000
THAT'S NOT FAIR.

696
00:50:48,000 --> 00:50:49,000
I'M SORRY, KATHY.

697
00:50:49,000 --> 00:50:50,000
AGREED, WE
LEAVE TONIGHT?

698
00:50:50,000 --> 00:50:52,000
YES.

699
00:50:52,000 --> 00:50:53,000
IT IS NOT AGREED.
YOU MUST STAY.

700
00:50:53,000 --> 00:50:56,000
I'M IN CHARGE HERE.
I TOLD YOU THAT BEFORE.

701
00:50:56,000 --> 00:50:58,000
THAT WAS IN YOUR
COUNTRY. WE ARE
NOW IN MINE.

702
00:50:58,000 --> 00:51:00,000
YOU CANNOT ESCAPE.

703
00:51:00,000 --> 00:51:02,000
EVERYWHERE, THE MEN
OF  TWALA  WATCH.

704
00:51:02,000 --> 00:51:04,000
ONE STEP BEYOND THAT
DOOR AND A SPEAR
WILL PIERCE YOUR BACK.

705
00:51:04,000 --> 00:51:06,000
HOW DO YOU
KNOW THAT?

706
00:51:06,000 --> 00:51:09,000
TOMORROW THE DRUMS BEAT,
THEY SMELL OUT THE EVILDOERS.

707
00:51:09,000 --> 00:51:11,000
GAGOOL WILL PUT HER MARK
ON THE ENEMIES OF THE KING.

708
00:51:11,000 --> 00:51:13,000
THEY DIE LIKE CATTLE.

709
00:51:13,000 --> 00:51:17,000
LOOKS LIKE A RED-
LETTER DAY FOR ALL
OF US, DOESN'T IT?

710
00:51:17,000 --> 00:51:18,000
YET THE PEOPLE ARE WEARY
OF WICKEDNESS AND BLOOD.

711
00:51:18,000 --> 00:51:21,000
IF THERE WAS ONE TO LEAD THEM,
THEY WOULD RISE UP.

712
00:51:21,000 --> 00:51:22,000
ISN'T THERE ONE?

713
00:51:22,000 --> 00:51:27,000
PERHAPS HE COULD BE FOUND.

714
00:51:28,000 --> 00:51:30,000
WHO ARE YOU?

715
00:51:30,000 --> 00:51:34,000
THE MAN WHO LOOKS
FOR DIAMONDS AND
HANGS ABOUT YOUR CAMP.

716
00:51:34,000 --> 00:51:38,000
THAT'S WHAT YOU SAID.

717
00:51:38,000 --> 00:51:40,000
ONCE THERE WAS
A KING IN THIS LAND,

718
00:51:40,000 --> 00:51:43,000
IMOTU THE LOVED,
BUT HE FOUGHT
THE WICKED GAGOOL,

719
00:51:43,000 --> 00:51:46,000
WHO IS OLDER THAN
THE MEMORY OF
THE OLDEST MAN.

720
00:51:46,000 --> 00:51:51,000
FOR THAT, SHE MADE HIS
BROTHER TWALA THE ONE-EYED
KILL HIM WHILE HE SLEPT.

721
00:51:51,000 --> 00:51:56,000
THE WIFE OF IMOTU
AND THE SON OF IMOTU
WERE DRIVEN INTO THE DESERT.

722
00:51:56,000 --> 00:51:59,000
IT IS SAID THEY DIED.

723
00:51:59,000 --> 00:52:04,000
IF THEY DIDN'T, THE
SON OF IMOTU SHOULD
BE KING AND NOT TWALA.

724
00:52:06,000 --> 00:52:09,000
YOU ARE THE
SON OF IMOTU.

725
00:52:09,000 --> 00:52:14,000
I AM THE
SON OF IMOTU.

726
00:52:14,000 --> 00:52:19,000
♪[Drums beating]

727
00:52:23,000 --> 00:52:28,000
[Whispering in Kukuana]

728
00:52:31,000 --> 00:52:36,000
♪[Drums beating, chanting]

729
00:52:55,000 --> 00:53:00,000
[Umbopa speaking Kukuana]

730
00:53:21,000 --> 00:53:23,000
THE COMMITTEE
SEEMS UNANIMOUS.

731
00:53:23,000 --> 00:53:26,000
I ALWAYS THOUGHT
THAT FELLOW HAD A SPOT
OF ROYAL BLOOD IN HIM.

732
00:53:26,000 --> 00:53:30,000
YOU DON'T GET A SNAKE
ON YOUR STOMACH
FOR NOTHING, YOU KNOW.

733
00:53:30,000 --> 00:53:31,000
IT IS AGREED.

734
00:53:31,000 --> 00:53:34,000
TOMORROW AT
THE SMELLING-OUT
OF THE EVILDOERS,

735
00:53:34,000 --> 00:53:37,000
THEY WILL LEAD
THE PEOPLE OF THE KUKUANA
AGAINST TWALA,

736
00:53:37,000 --> 00:53:39,000
BUT I NEED YOUR HELP.

737
00:53:39,000 --> 00:53:41,000
AND IN RETURN
I OFFER YOU YOUR LIVES

738
00:53:41,000 --> 00:53:44,000
AND THE FREEDOM OF THE MINES.

739
00:53:44,000 --> 00:53:46,000
FOR YOU, THE DIAMONDS, RICHES.

740
00:53:46,000 --> 00:53:49,000
FOR YOU, ADVENTURE.

741
00:53:49,000 --> 00:53:52,000
FOR YOU, THE HAPPINESS
OF THE  INKOOSIKAS.

742
00:53:52,000 --> 00:53:55,000
TODAY, YOU SAW
HOW TWALA TREATS STRANGERS.

743
00:53:55,000 --> 00:54:00,000
IF YOUR FATHER IS ALIVE,
HE IS IN THE MINE.

744
00:54:00,000 --> 00:54:02,000
HOW CAN WE HELP YOU?

745
00:54:02,000 --> 00:54:04,000
BEHIND TWALA
STANDS GAGOOL.

746
00:54:04,000 --> 00:54:07,000
THE PEOPLE FEAR
HER MAGIC.

747
00:54:07,000 --> 00:54:10,000
THEY WILL RISE ONLY
IF YOU SHOW THEM
A GREATER MAGIC.

748
00:54:10,000 --> 00:54:14,000
YOU LIVE AMONG US.
YOU KNOW THAT THE
WHITE MAN HAS NO MAGIC.

749
00:54:14,000 --> 00:54:16,000
I MUST HAVE MAGIC.

750
00:54:16,000 --> 00:54:17,000
AND IF WE CANNOT
GIVE IT?

751
00:54:17,000 --> 00:54:19,000
THE DRUMS WILL ROLL
AT THE SMELLING-OUT.

752
00:54:19,000 --> 00:54:21,000
GAGOOL WILL GIVE THE SIGN.

753
00:54:21,000 --> 00:54:24,000
THE KILLERS WILL SPEED
TO THE EVILDOERS.

754
00:54:24,000 --> 00:54:29,000
THEY WILL BEAT US TO DEATH.

755
00:54:29,000 --> 00:54:34,000
♪[Chanting, drums beating]

756
00:55:19,000 --> 00:55:21,000
FUNNY TO THINK IT'S
DERBY DAY BACK HOME.

757
00:55:21,000 --> 00:55:23,000
VERY FUNNY.

758
00:55:23,000 --> 00:55:26,000
I HAD A BET
ON MANITOBA.

759
00:55:26,000 --> 00:55:27,000
THERE'S NO SUCH HORSE.

760
00:55:27,000 --> 00:55:30,000
THERE CERTAINLY IS.
I'VE GOT IT IN MY DIARY.

761
00:55:30,000 --> 00:55:34,000
♪[Chanting]

762
00:55:34,000 --> 00:55:37,000
HERE IT IS,
DERBY DAY, MANI--

763
00:55:37,000 --> 00:55:40,000
BY JOVE! LOOK HERE!

764
00:55:40,000 --> 00:55:43,000
"11:15. TOTAL ECLIPSE OF
THE SUN VISIBLE OVER
TENERIFFE, SOUTH AFRICA."

765
00:55:43,000 --> 00:55:45,000
MAGIC!
GOOD, YOU'RE A GENIUS.

766
00:55:45,000 --> 00:55:47,000
11:15. THAT OUGHT
TO SETTLE 'EM, EH?

767
00:55:47,000 --> 00:55:50,000
IT'S A CHANCE.

768
00:55:50,000 --> 00:55:55,000
IF WE CAN HOLD OUT TILL 11:15.

769
00:56:38,000 --> 00:56:43,000
ARE YOU SURE IT'S
THIS YEAR'S DERBY?

770
00:56:43,000 --> 00:56:48,000
OF COURSE, I WOULDN'T HAVE
HAD A BET ON LAST YEAR'S
DERBY THIS YEAR, WOULD I?

771
00:56:48,000 --> 00:56:53,000
NO.

772
00:57:04,000 --> 00:57:05,000
[Shouts]

773
00:57:05,000 --> 00:57:07,000
[Drumming stops]

774
00:57:07,000 --> 00:57:08,000
[Shouts]

775
00:57:08,000 --> 00:57:11,000
[Crowd repeating chants
in Kukuana]

776
00:57:11,000 --> 00:57:16,000
♪[Rhythmic chanting]

777
00:57:23,000 --> 00:57:28,000
[Crowd]
OOOOHH!

778
00:57:43,000 --> 00:57:48,000
♪[Drums beating]

779
00:58:24,000 --> 00:58:29,000
♪[Drums beating faster]

780
00:58:35,000 --> 00:58:40,000
[Man screams]

781
00:58:46,000 --> 00:58:48,000
WHAT TIME IS IT?

782
00:58:48,000 --> 00:58:50,000
11:10.

783
00:58:50,000 --> 00:58:55,000
♪[Drums beating]

784
00:59:09,000 --> 00:59:14,000
♪[Drums beating faster]

785
00:59:19,000 --> 00:59:22,000
HOW LONG BEFORE
THEY GET TO US?

786
00:59:22,000 --> 00:59:27,000
A MATTER OF MINUTES.

787
00:59:30,000 --> 00:59:35,000
♪[Drums beating faster]

788
00:59:37,000 --> 00:59:39,000
[Man screams]

789
00:59:39,000 --> 00:59:44,000
NO SIGN OF
THE ECLIPSE YET.

790
00:59:53,000 --> 00:59:58,000
WE'RE NEXT.

791
01:00:05,000 --> 01:00:07,000
I HOPE I'M RIGHT
ABOUT THE TIME.

792
01:00:07,000 --> 01:00:12,000
GOD HELP US
IF YOU'RE NOT.

793
01:00:26,000 --> 01:00:31,000
♪[Drums beating faster]

794
01:00:42,000 --> 01:00:47,000
♪[Drums beating faster]

795
01:00:54,000 --> 01:00:59,000
[Speaking Kukuana]

796
01:01:10,000 --> 01:01:13,000
[Shouts]

797
01:01:13,000 --> 01:01:18,000
♪[Crowd chanting]

798
01:01:28,000 --> 01:01:33,000
[Speaking Kukuana]

799
01:01:51,000 --> 01:01:56,000
[Crowd screaming]

800
01:02:08,000 --> 01:02:13,000
♪ KUKUANA
KUKUANA ♪

801
01:02:13,000 --> 01:02:18,000
♪ KUKUANA

802
01:02:18,000 --> 01:02:21,000
♪ KUKUANA

803
01:02:21,000 --> 01:02:26,000
♪ KUKUANA

804
01:02:26,000 --> 01:02:29,000
♪ KUKUANA

805
01:02:29,000 --> 01:02:34,000
♪[Clapping and song
continuing in Kukuana]

806
01:02:36,000 --> 01:02:41,000
♪ KUKUANA

807
01:02:41,000 --> 01:02:46,000
♪ KUKUANA

808
01:02:47,000 --> 01:02:50,000
♪[Rhythmic drumming
and clapping]

809
01:02:50,000 --> 01:02:54,000
♪ KUKUANA

810
01:02:54,000 --> 01:02:58,000
♪ KUKUANA

811
01:02:58,000 --> 01:03:02,000
♪ KUKUANA

812
01:03:02,000 --> 01:03:04,000
♪ KUKUANA

813
01:03:04,000 --> 01:03:09,000
♪[Singing in Kukuana]

814
01:03:14,000 --> 01:03:17,000
♪ KUKUANA

815
01:03:17,000 --> 01:03:19,000
[Crowd]
♪ KUKUANA

816
01:03:19,000 --> 01:03:23,000
♪[Drumming]

817
01:03:23,000 --> 01:03:28,000
♪ KUKUANA

818
01:03:29,000 --> 01:03:34,000
♪[Drumming]

819
01:03:34,000 --> 01:03:39,000
[Shouting]

820
01:03:43,000 --> 01:03:48,000
♪[Drums beating]

821
01:04:02,000 --> 01:04:07,000
[Shouting]

822
01:04:20,000 --> 01:04:25,000
♪[Chanting]

823
01:05:06,000 --> 01:05:11,000
♪[Drum beating]

824
01:05:13,000 --> 01:05:18,000
[Shouts in the distance]

825
01:05:20,000 --> 01:05:25,000
[Shouting crowd approaches]

826
01:05:34,000 --> 01:05:35,000
[Umbopa]
WA!

827
01:05:35,000 --> 01:05:40,000
[Shouting]

828
01:05:42,000 --> 01:05:45,000
[Umbopa yelling]

829
01:05:45,000 --> 01:05:49,000
[Shouting]

830
01:05:49,000 --> 01:05:52,000
LAST TIME I FIRED
THIS THING,
IT DIDN'T FIRE.

831
01:05:52,000 --> 01:05:53,000
[Gun clicking]

832
01:05:53,000 --> 01:05:58,000
IT STILL
DOESN'T.

833
01:05:58,000 --> 01:05:59,000
[Shouting stops]

834
01:05:59,000 --> 01:06:03,000
[Mumbling]

835
01:06:03,000 --> 01:06:07,000
[Speaking Kukuana]

836
01:06:07,000 --> 01:06:12,000
[Shouting]

837
01:06:15,000 --> 01:06:20,000
[Shouts]

838
01:06:25,000 --> 01:06:30,000
♪[Chanting]

839
01:06:41,000 --> 01:06:46,000
[Shouting]

840
01:06:55,000 --> 01:06:57,000
♪[Chanting]

841
01:06:57,000 --> 01:06:58,000
[Shouting]

842
01:06:58,000 --> 01:07:03,000
[Shouting]

843
01:09:21,000 --> 01:09:26,000
[Screaming]

844
01:09:28,000 --> 01:09:33,000
[Silence]

845
01:09:42,000 --> 01:09:45,000
[Shouting in Kukuana]

846
01:09:45,000 --> 01:09:50,000
[Crowd repeating chant]

847
01:09:53,000 --> 01:09:56,000
KATHY? KATHY!
SHE'S GONE.

848
01:09:56,000 --> 01:09:58,000
LOOK!

849
01:09:58,000 --> 01:10:03,000
GAGOOL,
THE MINE!

850
01:10:30,000 --> 01:10:33,000
FATHER! FATHER! FATHER!

851
01:10:33,000 --> 01:10:36,000
FATHER!

852
01:10:36,000 --> 01:10:41,000
FATHER!

853
01:10:51,000 --> 01:10:56,000
FATHER!

854
01:11:00,000 --> 01:11:01,000
ARE YOU ALL RIGHT?

855
01:11:01,000 --> 01:11:03,000
INDEED, I'M
NOT ALL RIGHT,

856
01:11:03,000 --> 01:11:08,000
NOT AFTER
BREAKING ME LEG.

857
01:11:18,000 --> 01:11:23,000
[Rumbling]

858
01:11:29,000 --> 01:11:33,000
KATHY!

859
01:11:33,000 --> 01:11:37,000
KATHY!

860
01:11:37,000 --> 01:11:40,000
KATHY!
COME ON!

861
01:11:40,000 --> 01:11:43,000
OF COURSE YOU WOULD
BREAK YOUR LEG
IN A PLACE LIKE THIS.

862
01:11:43,000 --> 01:11:46,000
HOW DO YOU
EXPECT ME
TO CARRY YOU?

863
01:11:46,000 --> 01:11:48,000
YOU OLD DEVIL.

864
01:11:48,000 --> 01:11:53,000
KATHY! KATHY!

865
01:11:55,000 --> 01:12:00,000
COME ON, YOU CAN
GET THOSE LATER!

866
01:12:11,000 --> 01:12:13,000
KATHY!

867
01:12:13,000 --> 01:12:18,000
[Gurgling]

868
01:12:18,000 --> 01:12:19,000
[Hissing]

869
01:12:19,000 --> 01:12:22,000
DIDN'T I TELL YOU
HE'D GET HERE?

870
01:12:22,000 --> 01:12:23,000
THANK GOD
YOU'RE SAFE.

871
01:12:23,000 --> 01:12:25,000
OF COURSE
I'M SAFE.

872
01:12:25,000 --> 01:12:27,000
SO THIS IS WHAT
PUT AN END
TO THE MINES.

873
01:12:27,000 --> 01:12:29,000
THEY STUMBLED
UPON A VOLCANO.

874
01:12:29,000 --> 01:12:31,000
HOW DO YOU EXPLAIN
THOSE SKELETONS?

875
01:12:31,000 --> 01:12:35,000
MINERS TRYING TO ESCAPE
AND TRAPPED BY THE LAVA.

876
01:12:35,000 --> 01:12:40,000
OH... HURRY
UP, CURTIS,
WILL YOU?

877
01:13:07,000 --> 01:13:12,000
[Speaking Kukuana]

878
01:13:19,000 --> 01:13:24,000
[Screams]

879
01:13:30,000 --> 01:13:31,000
THIS IS
GOING, TOO!

880
01:13:31,000 --> 01:13:36,000
COME ON!

881
01:13:50,000 --> 01:13:53,000
TOO BAD THAT WHEN
WE GET TO A FORTUNE
IN DIAMONDS,

882
01:13:53,000 --> 01:13:56,000
THE MOUNTAIN
SHOULD DECIDE
TO SIT DOWN ON IT.

883
01:13:56,000 --> 01:13:58,000
IT DID NOT,
THEN.

884
01:13:58,000 --> 01:14:03,000
I'VE A FORTUNE
HERE IN ME POCKET.

885
01:14:03,000 --> 01:14:06,000
THERE'S ENOUGH
HERE FOR ALL OF US.

886
01:14:06,000 --> 01:14:11,000
DIAMONDS ARE NOT MUCH USE
WHEN YOU'RE TRAPPED
BEHIND SOLID ROCK.

887
01:14:11,000 --> 01:14:13,000
I DON'T WANT TO DEPRESS
YOU ANY FURTHER,

888
01:14:13,000 --> 01:14:16,000
BUT I THINK THERE'S
GOING TO BE AN ERUPTION.

889
01:14:16,000 --> 01:14:21,000
THAT FALL OF
ROCK, YOU KNOW?

890
01:14:21,000 --> 01:14:24,000
VOLCANOES ARE
NERVOUS THINGS,

891
01:14:24,000 --> 01:14:26,000
IT TAKES VERY LITTLE
TO UPSET THEM.

892
01:14:26,000 --> 01:14:31,000
[Explosions]

893
01:14:33,000 --> 01:14:38,000
IF IT WASN'T FOR ME,
YOU'D BE QUIETLY SHOOTING
GAME IN THE SOUTH.

894
01:14:38,000 --> 01:14:40,000
AND THEN YOU'D
HAVE GONE HOME

895
01:14:40,000 --> 01:14:42,000
AND MARRIED SOME NICE GIRL

896
01:14:42,000 --> 01:14:44,000
AND LIVED IN YOUR BIG HOUSE.

897
01:14:44,000 --> 01:14:48,000
AND SLOWLY GROWN
OLD AND FAT AND
DISAGREEABLE,

898
01:14:48,000 --> 01:14:52,000
AND ENDED UP A FEEBLE
OLD MAN WITH NO ONE
SORRY TO SEE YOU GO.

899
01:14:52,000 --> 01:14:56,000
NO, I'D RATHER
DIE YOUNG.

900
01:14:56,000 --> 01:14:59,000
STRANGE, I USED
TO HATE DYING.

901
01:14:59,000 --> 01:15:03,000
I'D LIE AWAKE AT NIGHT
THINKING ABOUT IT, SCARED.

902
01:15:03,000 --> 01:15:08,000
BUT WHEN YOU COME TO IT,
IT'S NOT SO BAD AFTER ALL.

903
01:15:08,000 --> 01:15:13,000
[Rumbling]

904
01:15:13,000 --> 01:15:18,000
[Explosions]

905
01:15:18,000 --> 01:15:21,000
THERE'S ONLY
ONE THING I'M
SORRY ABOUT.

906
01:15:21,000 --> 01:15:24,000
I'D LIKE TO HAVE
SEEN IRELAND AGAIN,

907
01:15:24,000 --> 01:15:27,000
THE GLEN OF ARMAGH
WHERE I WAS BORN,

908
01:15:27,000 --> 01:15:31,000
WITH THE MOUNTAINS
RUNNING DOWN
TO THE LAKES.

909
01:15:31,000 --> 01:15:34,000
WE WERE TO HAVE
GONE HOME NEXT YEAR.

910
01:15:34,000 --> 01:15:39,000
YOU COULD HAVE
COME WITH US.

911
01:15:40,000 --> 01:15:43,000
[Umbopa]
QUARTERMAIN!

912
01:15:43,000 --> 01:15:45,000
[Echoing]
QUARTERMAIN!

913
01:15:45,000 --> 01:15:50,000
[Echoing]
QUARTERMAIN!

914
01:15:50,000 --> 01:15:55,000
LOOK!
IT'S MOVING!

915
01:16:01,000 --> 01:16:03,000
GOOD IDEA BUT--

916
01:16:03,000 --> 01:16:07,000
IT--IT'S BOUND
TO FALL ON US.

917
01:16:07,000 --> 01:16:09,000
UMBOPA?

918
01:16:09,000 --> 01:16:14,000
[Umbopa]
CURTIS, WE MUST
PUSH IT CLEAR.

919
01:16:18,000 --> 01:16:19,000
READY?

920
01:16:19,000 --> 01:16:24,000
RIGHT.

921
01:16:34,000 --> 01:16:36,000
[Umbopa]
READY?

922
01:16:36,000 --> 01:16:41,000
THIS TIME.

923
01:16:49,000 --> 01:16:54,000
IT'S GONNA ERUPT!

924
01:17:02,000 --> 01:17:05,000
STEADY.
GOT HIM?

925
01:17:05,000 --> 01:17:10,000
[Rumbling]

926
01:17:22,000 --> 01:17:27,000
COME ON!

927
01:18:04,000 --> 01:18:07,000
